    "repair_message": "Complete this full-sweep recovery assignment. Restore relevant same-role ancestor cached reads before new reads; context lists selectable keys. For missing enumeration, read every missing subject/link page and explicitly account for all IDs. Use checkpoints after every page group; append only new rows. Do not submit an incomplete ledger. Assess canonical and rendered semantics without cosmetic rewrites. If legacy findings contradict evidence, correct or explicitly defer them. A new independent review remains mandatory. Exact previous rejection/validation error: Reviewer requested repair: [{\"defect\": \"The retained frame-zero predicate state_behavior gives an exhaustive two-way floating-point classification that is not exhaustive.\", \"fact_id\": \"fact:151272ec-1deb-477b-9dfe-51bb9a4d8cfa\", \"detail\": \"A failed <= comparison also includes unordered operands, not just input greater than the threshold. The proposal contains no replacement for this retained fact. State the actual accepted comparison and its false fallthrough, including NaN, rather than describing greater-than as the only rejection case.\", \"evidence\": [\"code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/src/melee/ft/kinds/ftCommon/ftCo_TurnRun.c#L31-L42\", \"code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/src/melee/ft/kinds/ftCommon/ftCo_Run.c#L125-L127\"]}, {\"defect\": \"The IASA state_behavior retention does not adequately preserve the exclusive Hammer branch.\", \"fact_id\": \"fact:b2ddc700-7b44-4e07-a1a2-b6bc2b41d9d0\", \"detail\": \"The baseline describes an ordered Hammer jump opportunity followed otherwise by ordinary input processing. Hammer possession instead returns the special selector's result immediately, including false; ordinary relaxed stick/button checks are not attempted. functionality.md correctly explains this, but the fact ledger retains the old claim and proposal.json has no corresponding correction.\", \"evidence\": [\"code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/src/melee/ft/kinds/ftCommon/ftCo_Jump.c#L62-L84\", \"code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/src/melee/ft/kinds/ftCommon/ftCo_HammerWait.c#L139-L146\", \"code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/src/melee/ft/kinds/ftCommon/ftCo_HammerJump.c#L15-L23\"]}, {\"defect\": \"Several retained collision claims promise the ordinary Fall state rather than the Fall entry dispatcher.\", \"detail\": \"ftCo_TurnRun_Coll always calls ftCo_Fall_Enter on a false collision result, but that callee has Master Hand, Crazy Hand, x2224_b2, and Hammer alternatives. The ledger declares all collision facts retained without this qualification. Narrow t. Previous artifacts are UNVALIDATED context, not evidence of correctness. Preserve supported findings while correcting defects. Original archived bytes: /Users/Ford/Github Repos/Codecaine/gamecube-decomp-harness/docs/.drafts/melee-semantic-20260908/main__melee__ft__kinds__ftCommon__ftCo_TurnRun/repair-history/full-resume-20260909-v1. Read previous artifacts as needed with sweep_read artifact using these paths: {\"coverage.json\": {\"artifact_path\": \"repair-history/full-resume-20260909-v1/coverage.json\", \"sha256\": \"1c558cfa9aa8e87cb9171f1b2788890fc8c26d1b3057d40ea230e7071e6d7774\"}, \"fact-dispositions.json\": {\"artifact_path\": \"repair-history/full-resume-20260909-v1/fact-dispositions.json\", \"sha256\": \"dac5dd12f0e877f5bed1fd61275891dcd41caad889cd9def64ce3b6ea33dfc7b\"}, \"functionality.md\": {\"artifact_path\": \"repair-history/full-resume-20260909-v1/functionality.md\", \"sha256\": \"6e3d075a28d34c8004120d3498bfd70708ea9c6ab678c49a12a1b17c2c757b2c\"}, \"link-dispositions.json\": {\"artifact_path\": \"repair-history/full-resume-20260909-v1/link-dispositions.json\", \"sha256\": \"c3b36000a139264c19db7cce32c7bb71d00c44af6a511e58a503be7ea8e9a348\"}, \"proposal.json\": {\"artifact_path\": \"repair-history/full-resume-20260909-v1/proposal.json\", \"sha256\": \"5e4b2580934b17a2160b22a65ae1cb0f8efc6d35c9228004